  "provenance": "Curated, auditable mapping of romanized Hindi/Hinglish anchor terms (from lexicon_mh_v1.json) and high-frequency code-mix function words to their Devanagari forms. Built for Stage 2 Part 2.1 (E2.1) as the OFFLINE, network-free, reproducible transliteration baseline that exploits MuRIL's Hindi-heavy pretraining (Mundra et al. 2025; Alakananda et al. 2025). The Google Translate API over the open vocabulary is the documented SCALE-UP path (locked E2.1: 'Google Translate API with offline fallback if feasible'). Versioned so it can be audited and cited.",
